  "Number": 20,
  "Question": "When \\(x^{13}+1\\) is divided by \\(x-1,\\) the remainder is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(-1\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(2\\)",
    "E": "None of these answers"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Because \\(x-1\\) has degree \\(1\\), the remainder must be a constant, say \\(r\\). Polynomial division gives an identity\n\\[\nx^{13}+1=(x-1)Q(x)+r\n\\]\nfor some polynomial \\(Q(x)\\).\n\nSubstituting \\(x=1\\) makes the entire quotient term vanish, leaving\n\\[\nr=1^{13}+1=2.\n\\]\nThe remainder is \\(\\boxed{2}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
